    <bpmn:process id="W_W1029" name="W1029. DC-Level Temperature, Humidity &amp; Environmental Monitoring for Sensitive Goods" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Continuous automated monitoring with alert thresholds; also triggered by seasonal planning (pre-summer, pre-rainy season)
Frequency: Continuous monitoring (24/7 × 365); monthly environmental report; quarterly system calibration
Volume: 4 DCs; ~50–200 sensor points per DC (temperature, humidity, air quality)
Owner: DC Operations Manager
Participants: DC Shift Supervisor, Quality Control Inspector, Maintenance Technician, Environmental Compliance Officer
Source: workflow W1029 — DC-Level Temperature, Humidity &amp; Environmental Monitoring for Sensitive Goods</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1029_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1029_Lane1" name="Maintenance Technician">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1029_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1029_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1029_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1029_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1029_Lane3" name="DC Shift Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1029_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1029_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1029_Lane4" name="Quality Control Inspector">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1029_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1029_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1029_Start6" name="Continuous automated monitoring with alert thresholds; also triggered by seasonal…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1029_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1029_Task7" name="Sensor Deployment &amp; Zone Configuration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Sensor Deployment &amp; Zone Configuration: DC is divided into environmental zones: (a) General warehouse: temperature target 20–35°C, humidity target 30–70%; (b) Paint &amp; chemical storage zone: temperature target 15–25°C, humidity target 30–60%, ventilation required; (c) Cement &amp; powder materials zone: humidity target &lt; 60%, sealed storage, no direct water exposure; (d) Battery &amp; electronics zone: temperature target 15–30°C, fire suppression system active, ventilation required; (e) Cold chain (if applicable): temperature target 15–25°C for specialty chemicals; (f) IoT sensors deployed per zone: temperature sensor (1 per 100 sqm), humidity sensor (1 per 200 sqm), air quality sensor (VOC/particulate, 1 per paint/chemical zone); (g) sensors transmit data to centralized environmental monitoring dashboard via Wi-Fi/LoRaWAN every 5 minutes
Responsible (R): Maintenance Technician / IT Infrastructure
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: Initial: 40–80 hours per DC; ongoing: 2–4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1029_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1029_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1029_Task8" name="Continuous Monitoring &amp; Automated Alerting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Continuous Monitoring &amp; Automated Alerting: Environmental monitoring dashboard provides real-time visibility: (a) Green (normal): all readings within zone target range; (b) Amber (warning): temperature or humidity approaching threshold (e.g., temperature within 2°C of upper limit); system sends alert to DC Shift Supervisor via mobile notification; (c) Red (critical): threshold exceeded (e.g., paint zone temperature &gt; 25°C, cement zone humidity &gt; 60%); system sends immediate alert to DC Shift Supervisor + DC Operations Manager + automated response trigger; (d) Black (emergency): hazardous condition detected (VOC spike in chemical zone indicating off-gassing, temperature &gt; 45°C in battery zone); system triggers fire alarm and evacuation protocol per W649
Responsible (R): System (IoT Sensors)
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: Continuous (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1029_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1029_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1029_Task9" name="Amber Alert Response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Amber Alert Response: DC Shift Supervisor responds to amber alert: (a) identify root cause: HVAC failure, dock door left open, external weather event, or sensor malfunction; (b) HVAC failure: contact maintenance for emergency repair per W650; deploy portable fans/dehumidifiers from emergency equipment stockpile; (c) Open dock door: close door immediately; train receiving staff on dock door discipline during temperature-sensitive zone operations; (d) External weather: during extreme heat (Philippine summer, April–May), pre-cool zones during early morning hours (4–6 AM) before peak heat; during rainy season, verify roof integrity and drainage per W798; (e) Sensor malfunction: Maintenance Technician verifies sensor reading with calibrated handheld device; if sensor is defective, replace and recalibrate per manufacturer instructions; (f) log response action and resolution time in system
Responsible (R): DC Shift Supervisor / Maintenance Technician
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 15–30 min per alert</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1029_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1029_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1029_Task10" name="Red Alert Response &amp; Product Protection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Red Alert Response &amp; Product Protection: DC Shift Supervisor responds to red alert: (a) immediately assess affected zone — is product integrity at risk? (b) Paint/chemical zone overheating: relocate temperature-sensitive pallets to cooler zone or staging area with portable cooling; check product for signs of degradation (bulging cans, separation, unusual odor); (c) Cement zone humidity breach: verify all cement pallets are wrapped in plastic sheeting; re-wrap any compromised pallets; inspect for clumping or hardening; (d) Battery zone overheating: activate additional ventilation; check Li-ion batteries for swelling or off-gassing per W1008 safety protocols; if any battery shows signs of thermal event, follow emergency protocol per W330; (e) log all product inspections with photos; system flags products with environmental exposure for quality hold pending inspection before shipment; (f) if product degradation confirmed: initiate inventory quality hold per W219 (Quarantine &amp; Recertification); damaged product dispositioned per W91 (Damaged/Defective Goods)
Responsible (R): DC Shift Supervisor / Quality Control Inspector
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 30–60 min per alert</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1029_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1029_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1029_Task11" name="Monthly Environmental Report &amp; Trend Analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly Environmental Report &amp; Trend Analysis: DC Quality Control Inspector compiles monthly report: (a) temperature and humidity compliance rate per zone (target: ≥ 95% within range); (b) number and duration of amber/red alerts; (c) root cause analysis of repeated alerts; (d) product quality incidents linked to environmental conditions; (e) HVAC system performance metrics (uptime, energy consumption); (f) trending: month-over-month, season-over-season comparison; (g) recommendations: zone reconfiguration, HVAC upgrade, insulation improvement, or operational changes; (h) report submitted to DC Operations Manager and VP Supply Chain for capital planning per W21
Responsible (R): Quality Control Inspector
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1029_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1029_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1029_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1029_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1029_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-252 (ensure controlled execution — DC Operations Management (PA-04.3).) | - operational: (heartbeat check — if sensor goes silent &gt; 15 minutes, alert generated)
Owner: DC Operations Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1029_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1029_Annotation13" targetRef="W1029_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1029_Flow15" sourceRef="W1029_Start6" targetRef="W1029_Task7" />
