    <bpmn:process id="W_W1041" name="W1041. DC-Level Outbound Quality Sampling &amp; Pre-Shipment Inspection" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Outbound shipment staged for dispatch; or triggered by receiving store&#x27;s quality complaint history
Frequency: Daily sampling at each DC; ~5–10 shipments/day inspected per DC
Volume: 4 DCs × 5–10 inspections/day = 20–40 inspections/day chain-wide
Owner: DC Quality Control Inspector
Participants: DC Pick/Pack Staff, DC Shift Supervisor, Store Receiving Clerk (feedback loop)
Source: workflow W1041 — DC-Level Outbound Quality Sampling &amp; Pre-Shipment Inspection</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1041_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1041_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1041_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1041_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1041_Lane2" name="DC Quality Control Inspector">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1041_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1041_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1041_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1041_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1041_Start4" name="Outbound shipment staged for dispatch; or triggered by receiving store&#x27;s quality…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1041_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1041_Task5" name="Sampling Selection &amp; Risk-Based Prioritization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Sampling Selection &amp; Risk-Based Prioritization: System selects shipments for quality inspection using risk-based sampling: (a) Mandatory inspection (100%): (i) first 3 shipments after new DC pick staff starts (training verification), (ii) shipments containing high-value items (&gt; PHP 10,000 per unit), (iii) shipments containing hazmat items per W236, (iv) shipments to stores with recent receiving quality complaints (store flagged in W666 with &gt; 3 quality complaints in past 30 days); (b) Random sampling (10% of remaining shipments): system randomly selects 10% of daily outbound shipments for inspection; (c) Targeted sampling: DC Quality Control Inspector may select additional shipments based on observed patterns (e.g., a specific picker&#x27;s error rate has increased, or a specific SKU category has had frequent errors)
Responsible (R): System / DC Quality Control Inspector
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 5–10 min/day (selection)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1041_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1041_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1041_Task6" name="Pre-Shipment Inspection Execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Pre-Shipment Inspection Execution: DC Quality Control Inspector inspects selected shipment: (a) verify pick accuracy: compare each picked item/quantity against pick list — scan each item barcode to verify correct SKU; count each item to verify correct quantity; (b) verify item condition: no visible damage (crushed packaging, broken seals, wet cartons, dented cans); (c) verify packaging: items packed securely for transit — heavy items on bottom, fragile items protected, no overhanging pallets, stretch wrap applied; (d) verify labeling: each carton labeled with correct store number, shipment number, and handling instructions; (e) verify load security: items loaded onto truck safely — no unstable stacking, weight distributed evenly, items secured with straps; (f) record results in system: pass (all items correct, undamaged, properly packed) or fail (detail the discrepancy — wrong item, wrong qty, damaged, improperly packed); (g) inspection pass rate target: ≥ 98%
Responsible (R): DC Quality Control Inspector
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 15–30 min per shipment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1041_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1041_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1041_Task7" name="Error Correction &amp; Root Cause Analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Error Correction &amp; Root Cause Analysis: For failed inspections: (a) DC Quality Control Inspector and DC Pick/Pack Staff correct the error immediately: (i) wrong item: replace with correct SKU; (ii) wrong quantity: add missing units or remove excess; (iii) damaged item: replace from inventory (damaged item routed to W91); (iv) improper packaging: repack correctly; (b) after correction, shipment reinspected before release for dispatch; (c) system logs error by: picker ID (who picked it), error type (wrong SKU, wrong qty, damage, packaging), SKU category, and store destination; (d) daily: DC Shift Supervisor reviews error log and identifies patterns: (i) specific picker with high error rate → retraining per W567 (Cross-Training), (ii) specific SKU category with recurring errors → evaluate storage/pick location (may need re-slotting per W784), (iii) specific time-of-day pattern → evaluate fatigue factor; (e) weekly: picker accuracy scorecard generated per employee for performance review per W796 (DC Workforce Productivity Tracking)
Responsible (R): DC Quality Control Inspector / DC Shift Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 10–15 min per error + 15–30 min/day (analysis)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1041_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1041_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1041_Task8" name="Store Feedback Loop &amp; Continuous Improvement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Store Feedback Loop &amp; Continuous Improvement: (a) store receiving quality feedback (from W666) feeds back to DC quality program: when a store reports a receiving discrepancy (wrong item, wrong qty, damage not caught at DC), the discrepancy is linked to the specific DC shipment and picker; (b) monthly: DC Quality Control Inspector compiles outbound quality report: (i) inspection pass rate (target ≥ 98%), (ii) error rate by type, by category, by picker, by store, (iii) store-reported discrepancy rate vs. DC inspection pass rate — gap indicates errors missed by inspection; (iv) trend vs. prior month; (c) quarterly: DC Operations Manager reviews quality program effectiveness: (i) has the outbound error rate decreased since program implementation? (ii) are we inspecting the right shipments? (adjust sampling methodology based on error patterns); (iii) ROI of quality program: cost of inspection labor vs. cost of outbound errors avoided (reduced store discrepancies, reduced shrinkage, improved customer availability)
Responsible (R): DC Quality Control Inspector / DC Operations Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2–4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1041_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1041_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1041_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1041_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1041_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-252 (ensure controlled execution — DC Operations Management (PA-04.3).) | - operational: DC Quality Control Inspector review and approval gate
Owner: DC Quality Control Inspector</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1041_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1041_Annotation10" targetRef="W1041_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1041_Flow12" sourceRef="W1041_Start4" targetRef="W1041_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1041_Flow13" sourceRef="W1041_Task5" targetRef="W1041_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1041_Flow14" sourceRef="W1041_Task6" targetRef="W1041_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1041_Flow15" sourceRef="W1041_Task7" targetRef="W1041_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1041_Flow16" sourceRef="W1041_Task8" targetRef="W1041_End9" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1041_diag">
