    <bpmn:process id="W_W1237" name="W1237. DC Value-Added Kit Assembly, Bundle Preparation &amp; Pre-Pack Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Kit/assembly work order generated from merchandise plan or promotional calendar
Frequency: Weekly; ~20–40 kit assemblies per week per DC
Volume: 4 DCs × ~30 kits/week = ~120 kits/week; ~6,240 kits/year
Owner: DC Operations Supervisor
Participants: DC Operations Supervisor, Stock Associate (Kit Assembly), Category Manager, Merchandise Analyst
Source: workflow W1237 — DC Value-Added Kit Assembly, Bundle Preparation &amp; Pre-Pack Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1237_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1237_Lane1" name="Merchandise Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1237_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1237_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1237_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1237_Lane2" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1237_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1237_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1237_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1237_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1237_Lane3" name="DC Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1237_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1237_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1237_Start5" name="Kit/assembly work order generated from merchandise plan or promotional calendar">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1237_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1237_Task6" name="Kit assembly work order creation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Kit assembly work order creation: Merchandise Analyst generates kit assembly work order: (a) specify kit SKU and quantity to assemble; (b) system explodes BOM per W46: lists all component SKUs and quantities required; (c) system checks component availability at DC; (d) reserve component inventory for assembly
Responsible (R): Merchandise Analyst
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 15 min/work order</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1237_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1237_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1237_Task7" name="Component picking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Component picking: Stock Associate picks component items from storage locations per WMS pick directive: (a) scan each component from storage bin; (b) verify quantity matches BOM; (c) stage components at kit assembly workstation
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): DC Supervisor
Duration: 15–30 min/kit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1237_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1237_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1237_Task8" name="Kit assembly &amp; quality check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Kit assembly &amp; quality check: Stock Associate assembles kit: (a) place all components into kit packaging; (b) verify all BOM items included (checklist); (c) apply kit barcode label; (d) quality check: all components present, undamaged, correct variant; (e) seal/secure kit packaging
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): DC Supervisor
Duration: 10–20 min/kit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1237_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1237_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1237_Task9" name="Kit receipt &amp; putaway">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Kit receipt &amp; putaway: (a) scan kit barcode to receive into inventory as kit SKU; (b) system consumes component SKUs from inventory (reduces component stock by BOM quantities); (c) system creates kit SKU inventory at received quantity; (d) putaway kit SKU to storage location per WMS directive
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): DC Supervisor
Duration: 5 min/kit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1237_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1237_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1237_Task10" name="Component shortage handling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Component shortage handling: If insufficient component stock: (a) system flags shortage during work order creation; (b) Merchandise Analyst decides: (i) defer assembly until component arrives, (ii) substitute component per W279 (requires BOM update), or (iii) partial assembly (assemble available kits); (c) update work order accordingly
Responsible (R): Merchandise Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1237_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1237_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1237_Task11" name="Kit disassembly (if needed)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Kit disassembly (if needed): For kit SKUs with slow movement or component shortage: (a) generate kit disassembly work order; (b) break kit back into component SKUs; (c) system reverses BOM consumption: component stock restored, kit stock reduced; (d) components returned to storage
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): DC Supervisor
Duration: 10 min/kit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1237_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1237_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1237_Task12" name="Weekly kit assembly reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Weekly kit assembly reporting: DC Supervisor reports: (a) kits assembled vs. planned; (b) component yield and waste; (c) assembly labor hours; (d) kit inventory levels vs. store demand
Responsible (R): DC Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1237_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1237_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1237_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1237_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1237_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-252 (ensure controlled execution — DC Operations Management (PA-04.3).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: DC Operations Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1237_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1237_Annotation14" targetRef="W1237_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1237_Flow16" sourceRef="W1237_Start5" targetRef="W1237_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1237_Flow17" sourceRef="W1237_Task6" targetRef="W1237_Task7" />
