    <bpmn:process id="W_W1241" name="W1241. DC Labor Shift Scheduling, Overtime Management &amp; Cross-Training Coordination" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Weekly labor planning cycle; also triggered by unexpected volume spikes (promotional surges, import container arrivals)
Frequency: Weekly planning; daily adjustments
Volume: 4 DCs × ~150 employees = ~600 DC staff across shifts
Owner: DC Manager
Participants: DC Manager, DC Supervisor, HR – Workforce Planning, Stock Associates, Forklift Operators, Receiving Clerks
Source: workflow W1241 — DC Labor Shift Scheduling, Overtime Management &amp; Cross-Training Coordination</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1241_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1241_Lane1" name="DC Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1241_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1241_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1241_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1241_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1241_Lane2" name="DC Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1241_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1241_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1241_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1241_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1241_Start4" name="Weekly labor planning cycle; also triggered by unexpected volume spikes (promotional…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1241_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1241_Task5" name="Weekly volume forecast">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly volume forecast: DC Manager receives weekly volume forecast from Supply Planning per W31: (a) expected inbound volume (vendor deliveries, import containers); (b) expected outbound volume (store replenishment orders); (c) special events (promotional dispatch, physical inventory per W42); (d) seasonal factors (typhoon season delays, holiday demand)
Responsible (R): DC Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1241_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1241_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1241_Task6" name="Shift schedule preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Shift schedule preparation: DC Supervisor prepares weekly shift schedule: (a) map staffing requirements per function (receiving, putaway, picking, packing, shipping, inventory control); (b) assign staff to shifts based on volume forecast; (c) ensure minimum staffing per function (e.g., at least 2 forklift operators per shift, 1 receiving clerk per dock door); (d) distribute overtime equitably across team
Responsible (R): DC Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1241_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1241_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1241_Task7" name="Overtime pre-approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Overtime pre-approval: (a) identify projected overtime needs for the week; (b) obtain DC Manager pre-approval for planned overtime; (c) for unplanned overtime (same-day spike): DC Supervisor requests verbal approval from DC Manager, followed by system confirmation; (d) system enforces maximum overtime limits per DOLE compliance per W10
Responsible (R): DC Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1241_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1241_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1241_Task8" name="Cross-training matrix maintenance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Cross-training matrix maintenance: DC Manager maintains cross-training matrix: (a) track which employees are certified for which functions (receiving, putaway, picking, packing, shipping, forklift, inventory); (b) identify cross-training gaps; (c) schedule cross-training sessions during low-volume periods; (d) target: every DC employee certified in ≥2 functions
Responsible (R): DC Manager
Accountable (A): HR – Workforce Planning
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1241_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1241_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1241_Task9" name="Daily attendance &amp; exception handling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Daily attendance &amp; exception handling: (a) biometric attendance tracked per W34; (b) DC Supervisor notified of absences/tardiness; (c) for unplanned absences: redeploy cross-trained staff from other functions; (d) if critical gap: call in off-duty staff with overtime approval; (e) system logs attendance exceptions for payroll per W10
Responsible (R): DC Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 15 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1241_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1241_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1241_Task10" name="Weekly labor cost review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Weekly labor cost review: DC Manager reviews: (a) actual labor hours vs. scheduled; (b) overtime hours and cost; (c) labor cost per unit processed (inbound + outbound); (d) cross-training utilization rate; (e) adjust next week&#x27;s schedule based on learnings
Responsible (R): DC Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1241_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1241_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1241_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1241_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1241_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-252 (ensure controlled execution — DC Operations Management (PA-04.3).) | - operational: DC Manager review and approval gate
Owner: DC Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1241_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1241_Annotation12" targetRef="W1241_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
