    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1428" name="W1428. DC Seasonal Surge Temporary Staffing, Onboarding &amp; Season-End Separation Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Seasonal demand surge forecast (S&amp;OP per W2); or DC capacity planning identifies staffing gap for upcoming peak season
Frequency: Bi-annual surge staffing cycles: (a) Mar–May (dry season construction peak + summer home improvement), (b) Sep–Dec (ber-months/Christmas peak); each surge lasting 2–4 months
Volume: ~30–50 temporary workers per DC per surge = 120–200 temporary workers across 4 DCs per surge event; 2 surges/year = 240–400 temporary worker lifecycles/year
Owner: DC Supervisor
Participants: DC Supervisor, HR Recruitment Specialist, HR Specialist (Payroll), Safety Officer, Training Coordinator, Workforce Planning Analyst
Source: workflow W1428 — DC Seasonal Surge Temporary Staffing, Onboarding &amp; Season-End Separation Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1428_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1428_Lane1" name="Workforce Planning Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1428_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1428_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1428_Lane2" name="HR Recruitment Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1428_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1428_Lane3" name="Safety Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1428_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1428_Lane4" name="DC Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1428_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1428_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1428_Start6" name="Seasonal demand surge forecast (S&amp;OP per W2); or DC capacity planning identifies staffing…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1428_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1428_Task7" name="Surge staffing planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Surge staffing planning (T-8 weeks): (a) Workforce Planning Analyst forecasts DC staffing needs per W652 (seasonal warehouse surge planning): (i) projected outbound volume increase per DC for upcoming season, (ii) translate to FTE needs: pickers, packers, loaders, forklift operators, (iii) identify skill requirements: forklift certification needed for 30% of temporary workers, (b) DC Supervisor submits staffing request to HR: number of temporary workers, start date, contract duration (typically 3–6 months), required skills, (c) HR Recruitment Specialist initiates recruitment per W19 (recruitment) with temporary/seasonal posting
Responsible (R): Workforce Planning Analyst / DC Supervisor
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1428_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1428_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1428_Task8" name="Rapid recruitment and selection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Rapid recruitment and selection (T-6 to T-4 weeks): (a) HR Recruitment Specialist sources temporary workers: (i) previous season&#x27;s temporary workers (re-hire reliable workers — reduces training time), (ii) local community recruitment (job posting near DC locations), (iii) manpower agency for bulk positions (laborers, pickers), (b) selection criteria: (i) physical fitness (DC work involves heavy lifting up to 25 kg), (ii) basic literacy (must read pick lists and labels), (iii) forklift operator certification (for forklift positions), (c) pre-employment requirements: (i) medical certificate (fit to work), (ii) SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG enrollment (mandatory even for project employees), (iii) signed project employment contract per Philippine Labor Code Article 297 (project employment)
Responsible (R): HR Recruitment Specialist
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 2–3 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1428_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1428_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1428_Task9" name="Expedited onboarding and safety training">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Expedited onboarding and safety training (T-1 to T-0): (a) Safety Officer conducts mandatory safety orientation (1 day): (i) DC safety rules, (ii) forklift/powered equipment awareness, (iii) hazmat handling basics (paint, chemicals per W1222), (iv) emergency evacuation procedures, (v) PPE requirements and issuance, (b) Training Coordinator provides DC operations orientation (1 day): (i) WMS/RF gun basics for pickers, (ii) pick path and bin location system, (iii) quality standards at pick and pack, (iv) attendance and timekeeping rules, (c) DC Supervisor assigns temporary workers to shift and team: paired with experienced permanent worker as mentor for first 2 weeks
Responsible (R): Safety Officer / Training Coordinator / DC Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Supervisor
Duration: 2 days/worker batch</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1428_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1428_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1428_Task10" name="Season-end separation processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Season-end separation processing (T+3 to T+6 months): When the seasonal surge ends: (a) DC Supervisor confirms seasonal volume has returned to baseline and temporary workers are no longer needed, (b) HR Specialist (Payroll) processes separation per W643 (final pay): (i) compute final pay including any pro-rated 13th month per W1416, (ii) return company property (uniforms, PPE, RF guns, access badges), (iii) clear any cash or inventory accountability, (c) documentation: (i) project completion certificate (confirming project employment has ended), (ii) clearance form signed by DC Supervisor (no pending accountability), (iii) certificate of employment issued per DOLE requirement, (d) HR Specialist flags high-performing temporary workers for priority re-hire in next surge cycle
Responsible (R): DC Supervisor / HR Specialist
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/worker</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1428_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1428_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1428_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1428_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1428_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-252 (ensure controlled execution — DC Operations Management (PA-04.3).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: DC Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1428_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1428_Annotation12" targetRef="W1428_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
