    <bpmn:process id="W_W1498" name="W1498. DC Temperature-Sensitive Material (Adhesives, Sealants, Paint) Storage Monitoring, Expiry Alert &amp; FIFO Enforcement" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Continuous IoT temperature monitoring; daily expiry scan; triggered when storage temperature deviates &gt; 5°C from manufacturer-recommended range for any SKU category
Frequency: Continuous temperature monitoring (24/7); daily expiry scan; monthly FIFO compliance audit
Volume: ~500–800 temperature-sensitive SKUs per DC; 4 DCs; estimated PHP 30–50M in temperature-sensitive inventory per DC
Owner: DC Operations Manager
Participants: Warehouse Associate, Quality Assurance Associate, DC Supervisor, Category Manager
Source: workflow W1498 — DC Temperature-Sensitive Material (Adhesives, Sealants, Paint) Storage Monitoring, Expiry Alert &amp; FIFO Enforcement</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1498_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1498_Lane1" name="DC Operations Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1498_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1498_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1498_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1498_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1498_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1498_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1498_Lane3" name="Quality Assurance Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1498_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1498_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1498_Start5" name="Continuous IoT temperature monitoring; daily expiry scan; triggered when storage…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1498_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1498_Task6" name="IoT temperature monitoring setup &amp; alerting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: IoT temperature monitoring setup &amp; alerting: (a) IoT temperature sensors installed in all temperature-sensitive storage zones: adhesive aisle, paint storage area, chemical storage cage; (b) sensors report temperature every 15 minutes to DC operations dashboard; (c) temperature thresholds configured per SKU category: (i) adhesives: max 30°C; (ii) paint: max 35°C (oil-based), 30°C (latex); (iii) chemicals: per SDS recommendation (varies); (d) if temperature exceeds threshold for &gt; 2 consecutive readings (30 min): (i) alert sent to DC Supervisor via SMS + dashboard; (ii) DC Supervisor investigates cause (HVAC failure, dock door left open, sensor malfunction); (iii) corrective action taken immediately; (iv) if temperature breach persists &gt; 4 hours: Quality Assurance Associate evaluates affected inventory per Step 3
Responsible (R): DC Operations Manager / IoT System
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1498_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1498_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1498_Task7" name="Daily expiry scan &amp; alert generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Daily expiry scan &amp; alert generation: Daily: (a) system scans all temperature-sensitive inventory for expiry status: (i) expired items: flagged for immediate removal and write-off; (ii) expiring within 30 days: flagged for priority dispatch (FIFO push to stores); (iii) expiring within 60 days: flagged for review — can it be sold before expiry?; (b) expiring items reported to DC Supervisor; (c) expired items physically pulled from storage and moved to quarantine area; (d) write-off initiated per PA-05.3 disposition workflow; (e) items expiring within 30 days: DC Supervisor coordinates with Merchandise Planner for expedited allocation to stores
Responsible (R): System / Warehouse Associate
Accountable (A): DC Supervisor
Duration: 30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1498_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1498_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1498_Task8" name="Temperature breach product quality evaluation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Temperature breach product quality evaluation: When temperature breach occurs: (a) Quality Assurance Associate identifies all SKUs that were stored in the affected zone during the breach period; (b) evaluates product integrity per manufacturer guidelines: (i) visual inspection (separation, discoloration, unusual viscosity for paint/adhesives); (ii) lot/batch number cross-referenced with manufacturer quality contact; (c) disposition decision: (i) &quot;Release&quot; — product quality unaffected; (ii) &quot;Quarantine&quot; — hold for further testing; (iii) &quot;Downgrade&quot; — sell at markdown with quality disclosure; (iv) &quot;Dispose&quot; — write-off as unsellable/unsafe; (d) disposition documented with QA Associate signature and DC Manager approval for write-offs
Responsible (R): Quality Assurance Associate
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours per incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1498_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1498_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1498_Task9" name="FIFO compliance enforcement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: FIFO compliance enforcement: (a) system enforces FIFO (First-In, First-Out) for all temperature-sensitive SKUs: (i) pick instructions always direct warehouse associate to the oldest lot first; (ii) if associate attempts to pick a newer lot when older stock exists: system blocks and prompts with older lot location; (iii) override requires DC Supervisor approval with reason code; (b) monthly FIFO compliance audit: (i) random sample of 50 temperature-sensitive picks reviewed for FIFO compliance; (ii) target: &gt; 98% FIFO compliance; (iii) non-compliance incidents tracked and addressed with associates
Responsible (R): System / Warehouse Associate
Accountable (A): DC Supervisor
Duration: Continuous + 2 hours/month audit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1498_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1498_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1498_Task10" name="Quarterly storage environment assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly storage environment assessment: Quarterly: (a) DC Operations Manager reviews: (i) total temperature breach incidents and duration; (ii) value of inventory affected by temperature damage; (iii) write-off value from temperature damage; (iv) HVAC system effectiveness and maintenance needs; (v) investment case for climate-controlled storage expansion if incidents exceed threshold; (b) recommendations submitted to VP Supply Chain for capital expenditure approval if infrastructure upgrades needed
Responsible (R): DC Operations Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1498_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1498_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1498_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1498_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1498_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-252 (ensure controlled execution — DC Operations Management (PA-04.3).) | - operational: DC Operations Manager review and approval gate
Owner: DC Operations Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1498_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1498_Annotation12" targetRef="W1498_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
